>
> The main question is this: should I still wish for Grayswandir?  

IMHO: No, for two reasons.  1) you don't need it, and 2) you're
unlikely to get it anyway.

There are many weapon choices available and Grayswandir is not the
only one.  If you're going to use the Tsurugi then make sure to keep
it blessed so that you don't end up with a cursed 2-handed weapon
welded to you.  If you're interested in silver sabers then either
polypile for them or else find some captains as you journey through
Gehennom.  Fully enchanted, your katana and Snickersnee is fine,
especially with MB for Elbereth engraving.  But don't believe me, do
the math for yourself using the weapons spoiler.  Or you could
continue to sacfest and you might end up with Grayswandir or Frostbane
that way.

As far as wishes go, I'd say that you're better off enchanting and
fooproofing your armor.  Use wishes on magic markers to write enchant
armor.  If you have destroy armor scrolls lying around use those when
cursed and confused to protect your armor.  Or you can write scrolls
of charging to charge up your wands of poly and use them to acquire
some useful scrolls and potions.

With wishes to burn, also consider saving one for an emergency.

Too bad about not having a neutral altar.  That gives you something to
wish for next time, though.
